# Trivy ignore file — accepted HIGH CVEs (0 CRITICAL) in the runtime images.
# Reviewed 2026-06-21 (see docs/production-readiness/risk-register.md PR-014). The Trivy gate is
# BLOCKING (deploy-checks.yml exit-code 1); every entry is an explicit, justified acceptance and the
# gate still FAILS on any NEW package/CVE not listed here (allowlist model, like .secrets.baseline).
#
# OS/debian base layers scan 0 HIGH/CRITICAL. All entries below are npm libraries.
#
# ── Build/CLI tooling deps that survive `npm prune --omit=dev` (npm-workspaces hoisting) ────────────
# `npm prune --omit=dev` in apps/{api,web}/Dockerfile drops most dev weight (per-image HIGH 13 -> 4),
# but npm hoists these transitive build-tooling deps (via jest / @nestjs/cli -> @angular-devkit /
# chokidar) into node_modules in a way prune does NOT fully remove. They are NOT on the request path
# (no user input is matched/globbed/temp-filed by the running service). 0 CRITICAL.
# FOLLOW-UP (real fix): do a clean prod-only install in the runtime stage
# (`rm -rf node_modules && npm ci --omit=dev`) so dev tooling is absent entirely, then drop these.
CVE-2025-64756
CVE-2026-44705
CVE-2026-33671
